From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:04:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: i2c: Document extcon detected hot-plugged I2C
 bus

Some accessories that sit on an I2C bus have no presence GPIO. The
Book Cover Keyboard of the Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 is an STMPE1801 key
matrix controller on the pogo pins, and only the SM5705 MUIC knows that
it is attached, from the 49.9 kOhm on the ID pin, which its extcon
driver reports as a dock.

Describe such a bus: like i2c-hotplug-gpio, with an extcon device in
place of the detect GPIO and its interrupt. The accessory's devices are
child nodes, so reference the I2C controller schema.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../bindings/i2c/i2c-hotplug-extcon.yaml      | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-hotplug-extcon.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-hotplug-extcon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-hotplug-extcon.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..82e7ab4e5cfb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/i2c/i2c-hotplug-extcon.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/i2c/i2c-hotplug-extcon.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Extcon detected hot-plugged I2C bus
+
+maintainers:
+  - Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
+
+description:
+  An I2C bus that runs to a connector, where the devices behind the
+  connector come and go with an accessory, and an extcon device reports
+  the accessory as a dock (EXTCON_DOCK). An example is a keyboard cover
+  on pogo pins that a USB interface controller recognises by the
+  resistance on its ID pin. The child nodes describe the accessory's
+  devices; they are added when the accessory is attached and removed
+  when it is detached.
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: /schemas/i2c/i2c-controller.yaml#
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: i2c-hotplug-extcon
+
+  extcon:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description: The extcon device that reports the accessory.
+
+  i2c-parent:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description: The I2C bus that the connector's I2C lines are on.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - extcon
+  - i2c-parent
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+
+    i2c-cover {
+        compatible = "i2c-hotplug-extcon";
+        extcon = <&muic>;
+        i2c-parent = <&pogo_i2c>;
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        keyboard@40 {
+            compatible = "st,stmpe1801";
+            reg = <0x40>;
+            interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
+            interrupts = <54 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+        };
+    };
+...
-- 
